  <!-- REVIEW (natural consequence) and CONTRAST PAIR with scenario 2.
       Deliberately the same sunburn as scenario 2 with the opposite answer.
       The difference is which behavior is in play: in 2 the action is putting
       on sunscreen (sunburn avoided -> NR), while here the action is falling
       asleep in the sun (sunburn added -> PP). Slide 41's note that "getting a
       sunburn is not an action, it is the result of inaction" is what forces
       that reading, and the explanation on this question points students back
       to scenario 2.

       Also a natural consequence, as with 3 and 10. -->
  <CapaProblem id="bmod_h2_scenario_16" title="16. Asleep in the Sun" showanswer="never">
    <KeyGrader id="bmod_h2_scenario_16_grader">
      <p>Sara falls asleep under the sun and gets a sunburn.</p>
      <ChoiceInput id="bmod_h2_scenario_16_input">
        <Distractor id="bmod_h2_scenario_16_pr">Positive Reinforcement</Distractor>
        <Distractor id="bmod_h2_scenario_16_nr">Negative Reinforcement</Distractor>
        <Key id="bmod_h2_scenario_16_pp">Positive Punishment</Key>
        <Distractor id="bmod_h2_scenario_16_np">Negative Punishment</Distractor>
      </ChoiceInput>
      <Explanation showWhen="answered"><Markdown>Behavior: *falling asleep in the sun* — this time the sunburn follows an action Sara took, so it is the consequence, not the behavior. She will do it less often (decrease), and a sunburn is **added**. Contrast this with the sunscreen scenario.</Markdown></Explanation>
    </KeyGrader>
    <DemandHints id="bmod_h2_scenario_16_hints">
      <Hint>Question 1: what is the behavior? It has to be an action the person takes, not something that happens to them.</Hint>
      <Hint>Question 2: will they do it MORE often or LESS often in future? More often is reinforcement; less often is punishment.</Hint>
      <Hint>Question 3: after the behavior, is something ADDED or TAKEN AWAY? Added is positive; taken away is negative — including something unpleasant that is avoided or escaped.</Hint>
    </DemandHints>
  </CapaProblem>

  <CapaProblem id="bmod_h2_scenario_17" title="17. Lever and Shock" showanswer="never">
    <KeyGrader id="bmod_h2_scenario_17_grader">
      <p>A rat presses a lever and gets a shock.</p>
      <ChoiceInput id="bmod_h2_scenario_17_input">
        <Distractor id="bmod_h2_scenario_17_pr">Positive Reinforcement</Distractor>
